<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">23 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 23 August, from 406 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">406 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,620 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stilicho executes the Gothic leader Radagaisus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Having trapped Radagaisus's invading army near Faesulae, the Roman general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stilicho">Stilicho</a> had the Gothic king executed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> was saved for now, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s frontiers were under mounting pressure.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/odoacer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/476">476 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,550 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Odoacer is proclaimed king by the foederati in Italy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orestes-roman-general">Orestes</a> refused the Germanic foederati land in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, they and much of the Italic Roman army proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> king. He then deposed the young emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus">Romulus</a>, a takeover traditionally seen as the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1268">1268 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">758 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles of Anjou defeats Conradin at Tagliacozzo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Using a hidden reserve, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles I of Anjou</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conradin">Conradin</a>, the sixteen-year-old last heir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>, who had come to reclaim the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>. Conradin was captured and beheaded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> that October, ending Hohenstaufen rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tagliacozzo">Battle of Tagliacozzo</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conradin">Conradin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles I of Anjou</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1305">1305 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">721 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Wallace is executed in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Betrayed and captured near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-wallace">William Wallace</a> was hanged, drawn and quartered at Smithfield. The victor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a> Bridge became an enduring symbol of Scottish independence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1382">1382 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">644 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tokhtamysh of the Golden Horde lays siege to Moscow</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serpukhov">Serpukhov</a>, the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhtamysh">Tokhtamysh</a>, khan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>, besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, which Grand Prince Dmitrij had left under the Lithuanian prince Ostej. Three days later the citizens were tricked into surrendering, and the city was stormed and razed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jochids">Jochids</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1572">1572 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">454 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French court resolves to kill the Huguenot leaders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the eve of St Bartholomew's Day, Charles IX and his council agreed to eliminate the Protestant leaders gathered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. The killings began before dawn and spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nazi Germany and the Soviet Union sign a non-aggression pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ribbentrop and Molotov signed a pact in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> whose secret protocol divided eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> into spheres of influence. It cleared the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> a week later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Two million people form the Baltic Way human chain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some two million people joined hands across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>, Latvia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> on the 50th anniversary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molotov-ribbentrop-pact">Nazi-Soviet Pact</a>. The 675 km chain demanded independence, regained in 1990-91.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a></div></div></li></ol>
